<p>
  They told you to be a warrior.<br>
  But they never sat you down and told you who you were supposed to be fighting.<br><br>

  So you figured it out yourself.<br>
  You thought the enemy was out there.<br><br>
  
  So you picked up a sword, any sword would do: anger, ambition, revenge.<br>
  You didn't care what it was called,br
  as long as it was heavy enough to swing.<br>
  And you swung.<br>
  And God, you swung.<br>
  And you won again and again and again.<br><br>

  But the war never ended,<br>
  because you were bleeding in the wrong place.<br><br>

  The battlefield was never out there, son.<br>
  It was in here.<br><br>

  A true warrior has no enemies,<br>
  not because no one can touch him,<br>
  but because ...
</p>

